                <pb facs="0662" n="586" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg586"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5631/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">The
                                Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-20T16:00:00+01:19">June 20, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 20—12:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Department’s telegram No. 26, June 19, 7 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d476-f1"
                    /> Original plan of instructing Legation in Washington to enter into further
                    preliminary conversations has been changed. Decision reached last night in
                    Cabinet sub-committee to send Lamping or substitute to Washington in the first
                    week of July for the purpose of a short preliminary discussion. He will be
                    accompanied by a representative of the East Indies. They consider that questions
                    of general policy should receive further attention before actual
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Emmet</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
